rooms_desc ({"This room serves as an initial reception area for Blaarg andKarisma's guests. As one looks around, one gets an impression of an oldbed&breakfast in New England. The floors are hardwood, polished, with atraditional throw rug in the center. The walls are wainscoted up to waistlevel with dark-stained oak, and above it the walls are painted antiquewhite. There is a chandelier hanging from the ceiling, and there is apicture hanging from the north wall.","This is the main hallway. The oak wainscoting and the antique whitewalls continue, but now there are gas lamps placed at evenintervals along either side of the hallway. The lamps are extremely old, but still function, and are used to light thehallway at night. To the west is the guest room, to the east is the master bedroom, to the south is the foyer, and to thenorth is the rose garden.","The New England motif continues with this room, the masterbedroom. The walls are decorated with pictures of Blaarg'sfriends, and on the floor is am oriental throw rug. Onthe northern side of the room is an antique oak sleighbed, and on the southern side is a marble fireplace, where Blaarg can make this room even more cozy. To the east, French doors open out onto a deck with a wonderful view. Why don't you go out there and see? ","As you walk into this room, you are hit with the wonderful aroma of roses...then you see why. This is Blaarg's rose garden...a place for him to relax and get immersed in the beautyof nature. White and red roses are prevalent, but you see some pink and yellow ones too. The beauty of thisgarden is enough to strike awe in the most hard-heartedfighter...Feel free to pick one or just smell them all.....","This is where Blaarg's guests sleep when they come to visithim. The New England walls continue in this room, and thereis no throw rug in order to show off the hardwood floors. Theguests sleep in a four-poster bed, and have a wonderful view of the valley in the western window. ","As you walk through the french doors, you are overwhelmed by the beauty of the view that standing on the deck offers you. Just off the deck is a beautiful blue lake, reflecting the image of a snow-capped mountain in the background. Surrounding the lake are enormouspine trees which are also reflected in the lake's image. As youlook to the east, you can tell that the sunrises must be spectacular.","this room holds blaarg's equip.",0,0,0,})
